@startuml Push Notification Service - Activity Flow Diagram

start

:Client sends HTTP request\n(POST /push/all);

:Elysia receives request\nand parses JSON body;

:Auth Middleware extracts\nAuthorization header;

if (Valid Bearer Token?) then
  :Load authenticated admin\ncontext from token;
else
  :Use default SUPER_ADMIN\ncontext (dev mode);
endif

:Validation Middleware\nvalidates request payload;

if (Valid payload?) then
else
  :Return 400 Bad Request\nwith validation errors;
  stop
endif

:ViewModel checks admin\nrole permissions;

if (Has required role?) then
else
  :Return 403 Forbidden\nInsufficient permissions;
  stop
endif

:Campaign Model creates\nnotification campaign\nwith DRAFT status;

:For each locale in request\nCreate NotificationContent\nrecords with title, body,\nicon_url, action_url;

if (All content created?) then
else
  :Rollback transaction\nReturn 500 error;
  stop
endif

:Subscription Model queries\nactive web push subscriptions\nbased on target (all/user/segment/topic);

if (Found subscriptions?) then
  :For each subscription\nLog delivery attempt\nwith HTTP status code;
else
  :Continue without subscribers\n(valid for new deployments);
endif

:Update campaign status\nbased on scheduled_at:\n- If scheduled_at: QUEUED\n- If null: SENDING;

:Return 201 Created response\nwith campaign_id\nand total_subscribers;

:API client receives response\nand logs the operation;

stop

note right
  **Error Handling:**
  - Invalid auth → 401
  - Invalid role → 403
  - Invalid payload → 400
  - Database errors → 500
  - DB constraint violation → 500
end note

note right
  **Campaign Lifecycle:**
  DRAFT → QUEUED → SENDING
       → COMPLETED/FAILED
end note

@enduml
